  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreS&E 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After multiple lab experiments, a research team plans to use animal
    models to study how a potential new cancer treatment affects the body.


    <b>Which
    group reviews and approves in vivo preclinical studies to ensure the study is
    justified and animals are treated humanely?</b>'
  explanation: The IACUC reviews all animal research to ensure it is truly necessary,
    uses the fewest animals possible, and includes steps to reduce pain or distress.
    Their oversight protects animal welfare and helps ensure studies are conducted
    ethically and responsibly before research moves closer to human trials.
  correctAnswer: Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC)
  incorrectAnswer1: Institutional Review Board (IRB)
  incorrectAnswer2: Data and Safety Monitoring Board (DSMB)
  incorrectAnswer3: Food and Drug Administration (FDA)
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
